Well, that rather understates the issue.

Monsters aren't merely "tougher", they
are "tougher at specific waypoints".

You have to face tougher monsters to
explore Mines Town; usually, much
tougher.

You have to face tougher monsters to
recover the luckstone.

You have to face tougher monsters to
consult the oracle.

You have to face tougher monsters to
enter Sokoban, and to clean out the
treasure zoo at the top.

And on and on. All of these goals,
except entrance to your quest, are
easier if the PC minimizes rather than
maximizing XL.

Because you've cut down the protection
you can afford in Mines Town, you have
to suffer through all this with an inferior
AC as well as the monsters being tougher.
That compounds the problem.

